'''Joint Base Ajowa''' ({{Langx|kz|ߌߟߋ ߊߜ߭ߊ ߊߖߐߥ|Ilé Agha Àjòwà|Ajowa house of war}}) is a [[W:Naval air station|naval air station]] in the [[Ajowa|Ajowa district]] of [[Sanyan]], housing military personnel from the [[Concepción Organization of Co-Operation]]. 

The base was originally established in 1837 following Balisca's ratification of the [[Kafto-Ethiopian Charter]], after which it played a crucial role in the [[Kaftian anti-slave trade campaign]]. Following the signing of the [[Mutual Arms and Technology Agreement]] (MATA) in the aftermath of the 1977 [[Bight of Ayorin Crisis]], the base underwent significant expansion to accommodate additional personnel and equipment, along with additional security upgrades and facilities.

